1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,800
Ever read the same sentence three times

2
00:00:03,820 --> 00:00:05,849
and still have no idea what it said?

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,020
That feeling is often called brain fog—

4
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:13,029
and it's a common complaint after a

5
00:00:13,049 --> 00:00:13,661
concussion.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,311
It can feel like your thoughts are slower,

7
00:00:19,331 --> 00:00:20,810
your memory isn't as sharp,

8
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:22,975
or it takes more effort to concentrate.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,252
And brain fog isn't the same thing as

10
00:00:32,272 --> 00:00:34,462
being lazy or simply not trying hard

11
00:00:34,482 --> 00:00:34,892
enough.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,599
After a concussion, the brain may have a

13
00:00:43,619 --> 00:00:46,088
harder time efficiently processing and

14
00:00:46,108 --> 00:00:47,725
coordinating information.

15
00:00:47,745 --> 00:00:50,148
Tasks that used to feel automatic can

16
00:00:50,168 --> 00:00:52,374
suddenly require much more effort.

17
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,258
That's why a busy day can sometimes leave

18
00:00:57,278 --> 00:00:58,980
you feeling completely drained—

19
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,925
even when you haven't done anything

20
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:02,092
physically demanding.

21
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,447
If brain fog is getting in the way of your

22
00:01:09,467 --> 00:01:11,326
day, don't just push through it.

23
00:01:11,346 --> 00:01:13,675
Your brain may need the right evaluation

24
00:01:13,695 --> 00:01:14,732
and recovery plan.

